    "html": "<p>v0.0.15 cut on 2026-10-24, carrying two rounds that closed the landing page&#39;s last honest gaps: <strong>every capability in the dex is now filmed</strong>, and the creature artwork passed its own machine review. This post is the release-note longhand — the changelog stop and the GitHub release carry the itemized record; this one explains what the two rounds mean.</p>\n<h2>The media-completion round</h2>\n<p>The capability dex had a standing contract: a capability without footage ships with an honest empty stage — a &quot;pending&quot; plate that says so. As of this release, <strong>the dex ships 24 movies on 22 entries, zero stills, zero pending</strong> — every entry carries a real captured reel, and the gates were hardened from &quot;pending plates are stated honestly&quot; to &quot;no plate may ship unfilmed.&quot;</p>\n<p>The last two plates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>№ 010 Parity</strong> (the SDLC checklist) — one real task drives the session through <code>/context</code> and the session workflow end to end: <code>/sessions list</code> → <code>/sessions export --md</code> → the exported file on disk → <code>/sessions list --all</code>. The poster is the sessions list itself: the face of the workflow.</li>\n<li><strong>№ 011 Browser</strong> (the browser subagent) — the moving cut that retires the older PTY stills: the sync delegation row (<code>task → browser</code>), the humanized live tool labels riding it, the child&#39;s report quoting live confirmation text from a real rendered page, then the async lane — the fleet widget row and the <code>/tasks</code> lifecycle registry.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The arithmetic is pinned by tests: <code>24 = 22 + 2</code> (twenty-two single-reel entries plus the browser entry&#39;s two labelled reels), and three suites fail if a pending plate ever returns.</p>\n<h2>The sprite craft round</h2>\n<p>The creature sprites are authored pixel art produced by a deterministic pipeline — the script is the art. This round the atlas&#39;s own VLM review lane returned <strong>FIX</strong> with three concrete craft defects, all repaired in the atlas code and re-gated:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>memory</strong> (the archive turtle) — the retrieved card floated six rows above the drawer, reading as a detached fleck; it now rides the drawer mid-pull, outline wrapping card and drawer as one shape.</li>\n<li><strong>mcp</strong> (the socket golem) — the floating head read as a glitch; a centered gold energy column now bridges head to collar, and the chest sockets and treads read as recessed ports and segments rather than buttons and a skirt.</li>\n<li><strong>lsp</strong> (the bookwyrm) — the touching spectacle rings read as one gold mask; an explicit bridge bar plus temple arms make them read as glasses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The review lane&#39;s verdict is now <strong>PASS</strong> with IP-safety clean, and all eleven sprites re-gated through the pipeline&#39;s own integrity checks (edge outlines, orphan clusters, the 5-bit GBA grid, colour budget, dark ratio).</p>\n<h2>What else the release verified</h2>\n<p>Like every release, this one ran the full verification matrix before the tag: the engine suite green across the board, the integration suite and the bridge suite, the release-artifact plan gate, the six per-OS standalone binaries built with the linux-x64 archive extracted and executed locally (<code>unown --version</code> → 0.0.15), the landing production build plus standalone smoke, the full e2e walk with the video-decode gate stepping through all 24 movies, and the 3-OS release matrix the tag triggers.</p>\n<h2>Where to verify it yourself</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The changelog stop: <a href=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\"><code>v0.0.15</code> in CHANGELOG.md</a> — the itemized record this post summarizes.</li>\n<li>The GitHub release: <a href=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/releases/tag/v0.0.15\">v0.0.15</a> — the six per-OS binaries, <code>sha256sums.txt</code>, SBOM.</li>\n<li>The dex itself: scroll to the capability dex on the <a href=\"https://unown-nine.vercel.app/#dex\">landing page</a> and click through — every reel there is one of the 24.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Release posts stay media-light on purpose: the feature posts carry the captures, the changelog carries the itemization, and this post is the connective tissue between them.</p>\n"
